TUTORIALS.append({'title': 'VIN-1. Setup: folders, INSTALLED_APPS, urls, the data', 'category': 'programming', 'order': 1, 'summary': 'Do this first: the app layout, settings and where the data goes.', 'content': '<p>Step 1 of 11. Create the app folder with this layout. The three <code>__init__.py</code> files are empty. Add <code>"vintage"</code> to <code>INSTALLED_APPS</code> and include its urls. There are no models, so no migrations.</p>\n<p>Needs <code>polars</code>, <code>numpy</code> and <code>openpyxl</code> (Excel). Put your parquet file(s) into <code>BASE_DIR/datasets/vintage/input/</code> — every <code>*.parquet</code> there is read. Columns: <code>anketa</code>, <code>report_date</code> (1st of the month = the previous month), <code>valuedate</code>, <code>maks_dni</code>, <code>npl_category</code>, <code>brutto_95_summa</code>, <code>given_amount</code> and <code>passport</code> (pervichka / vtorichka): everything is built for all passports together and for each one, and the pages switch between them. If yours are named differently, change the right-hand side of <code>COLUMNS</code> at the top of <code>process.py</code>.</p>\n<p>Then press «Пересчитать» on <code>/vintage/</code> (it runs the command in its own process, the page refreshes itself), or run it by hand:</p>\n<pre><code class="language-bash">python manage.py build_vintage          # your files\npython manage.py build_vintage --fake   # fake data first, only if the folder is empty\n</code></pre>\n<p>Try <code>--fake</code> first to see every page; then delete <code>fake.parquet</code> and put the real file in.</p>\n<p>Sidebar link in base.html: <code>{% url \'vintage\' %}</code>, icon <code>fa-solid fa-layer-group</code>.</p>\n<h3>Layout</h3>\n<pre><code class="language-plaintext">vintage/\n    __init__.py\n    management/__init__.py\n    management/commands/__init__.py\n    apps.py\n    urls.py\n    process.py\n    fake.py\n    management/commands/build_vintage.py\n    views.py\n    templates/vintage/style.html\n    templates/vintage/page.html\n    templates/vintage/plan.html\n    templates/vintage/chart.html\n</code></pre>\n<h3>urls.py of the project</h3>\n<pre><code class="language-python">path("vintage/", include("vintage.urls")),\n</code></pre>\n'})

